# alioth-loud :: SELinux rules
#
# Deliberately empty of active rules.
#
# Layer 4b writes to smart-amplifier sysfs nodes. Whether that needs a policy
# exception depends entirely on the label the kernel gives those nodes, which
# differs per driver (aw882xx, cs35l41, tfa98xx all label differently) and per
# ROM. Guessing means either a rule that does nothing, or a rule far broader
# than necessary.
#
# The probe script captures the labels. Once we know them, the correct rule is
# narrow, e.g. for an Awinic amp exposing nodes as sysfs_aw882xx:
#
#     allow magisk sysfs_aw882xx dir  { search }
#     allow magisk sysfs_aw882xx file { open read write getattr }
#
# and on KernelSU/APatch the source domain is su rather than magisk:
#
#     allow su sysfs_aw882xx file { open read write getattr }
#
# Do not replace these with `allow magisk sysfs file *`. That grants write
# access to every sysfs node on the device for the lifetime of the module,
# which is a much bigger hole than this feature warrants.
#
# If layer 4b logs "write failed (selinux?)", get the label with:
#     ls -Z <node>
# and add the matching narrow rule here.
